---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAILS, MARKETING_SITE_URL } from "../lib/site";

const sections = [
  ["scope", "Scope"],
  ["website-data", "Website data"],
  ["local-software", "Local software"],
  ["communications", "Communications"],
  ["sharing", "Sharing and retention"],
  ["rights", "Your rights"],
  ["changes", "Changes"],
  ["contact", "Contact"],
] as const;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Privacy Policy — Not Codex"
  description="Privacy information for the Not Codex public website and source project."
  heading="Not Codex Privacy Policy"
  lede="This policy explains the limited information associated with the public website and project. Not Codex does not currently operate a public hosted app, account system, paid service, or Connect service."
  effectiveDate="2026-07-21"
  lastUpdated="2026-07-21"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="scope">
    <p class="section-number">01</p><h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>This policy applies to <a href={MARKETING_SITE_URL}>{MARKETING_SITE_URL}</a> and direct communications with Yossi Elkrief, operating under the MaTrixy and BPro names. GitHub and any hosting, DNS, email, coding-agent, or package provider process information under their own policies.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="website-data">
    <p class="section-number">02</p><h2>Website data</h2>
    <p>The Site is a static website. It does not intentionally set analytics, advertising, or account cookies. The hosting and network providers may process ordinary request data such as IP address, user agent, requested path, timestamps, and security diagnostics to deliver and protect the Site.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="local-software">
    <p class="section-number">03</p><h2>Local software</h2>
    <p>When you build and run Not Codex yourself, project data, prompts, credentials, and agent activity are handled by your device and the providers you configure. We do not receive that data merely because you use the source code. Features you independently configure may communicate with third parties as documented in the repository.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="communications">
    <p class="section-number">04</p><h2>Communications</h2>
    <p>If you email us or submit a report, we receive the information you provide and related delivery metadata. Do not send secrets or private source unless a secure channel has been agreed. Public GitHub issues and discussions are visible according to GitHub’s settings.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="sharing">
    <p class="section-number">05</p><h2>Sharing and retention</h2>
    <p>We use service providers as needed to host the Site, repository, DNS, and email. We may disclose information when required by law or to protect people, rights, and systems. We do not sell personal information. We retain communications and operational records only as reasonably needed for support, security, legal obligations, and project administration.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="rights">
    <p class="section-number">06</p><h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, or object to processing of your personal information. Email the privacy address below. We may need enough information to verify and complete the request.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="changes">
    <p class="section-number">07</p><h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>We will update this policy before introducing materially different public data practices, such as hosted accounts or telemetry, and will change the date above.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="contact">
    <p class="section-number">08</p><h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Privacy requests: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAILS.privacy}`}>{CONTACT_EMAILS.privacy}</a>. Operator: Yossi Elkrief, operating under the MaTrixy and BPro names, Israel.</p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
